[[:db/retract 17592186194940 :answer-field/choices 17592186194941] {:db/id 17592186198272 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-69e168c4-5f9a-5e25-9886-56938c3e22bc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-69e168c4-5f9a-5e25-9886-56938c3e22bc" :question/id #uuid "69e168c4-5f9a-5e25-9886-56938c3e22bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-184493" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S={-1,2,3}\\times (0,1)$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS={-1,2,3}\\times (0,1)\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is either $-1,2,$ or $3$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $(0,1).$\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\,:\\,x{-1,2,3},\\,y\\in (0,1)}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $-1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $(0,1).$\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}={(-1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in (0,1)}\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/1e/1e09e88b9f8bd472c1fd74b4d77a7aefff9b1170787899bc78fcf56e79518436.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $2$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $(0,1).$\n\n$$\n{S}_{2}={(2,y)\\,:\\,y\\in (0,1)}.\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/3f/3f4ecac159eba9f49d6745ac2a46956fd19b68f0520974a6c618ebc1f118588a.png)\n\nNow, consider ${S}_{3}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $3$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $(0,1)].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{2}={(3,y)\\,:\\,y\\in (0,1)}.\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/96/969ee218899817fe5bf497369fb6b2e5fa360fba0fbd4733c442c42208fa566c.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\nS={S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\\cup {S}_{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $S$ can be represented by the three line segments shown below.\n\n![](images/7f/7f0ad1b126502e27710bcc97a72c4eec889a74f7f6dfac6449d98710ea16e16b.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a0679b83-eb07-56b2-8627-6297e6d7c5c2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a0679b83-eb07-56b2-8627-6297e6d7c5c2" :answer-field/id #uuid "a0679b83-eb07-56b2-8627-6297e6d7c5c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e4ee8d17-5a63-5173-8b8a-3df477a3214a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5c7fddcc-19ee-56b6-868e-3da3bcc7ff9b" "answer-99783709-ffe5-578d-88da-9f3f0a723a52" "answer-a567a8e6-cc8d-54d0-8bad-c679c940a138" "answer-e4ee8d17-5a63-5173-8b8a-3df477a3214a" "answer-d4fc3416-aa9f-553e-b04b-84e342d586ab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c7fddcc-19ee-56b6-868e-3da3bcc7ff9b" :answer/id #uuid "5c7fddcc-19ee-56b6-868e-3da3bcc7ff9b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/2b/2bcbcbb5a632f21d19777d050a9a8897b8659003dc26a57e753efd412640c442.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99783709-ffe5-578d-88da-9f3f0a723a52" :answer/id #uuid "99783709-ffe5-578d-88da-9f3f0a723a52" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/74/741031b9897b9a0fe0a43238976fcc3d22ba0ca15bbd427d63a3e9c6392006c5.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a567a8e6-cc8d-54d0-8bad-c679c940a138" :answer/id #uuid "a567a8e6-cc8d-54d0-8bad-c679c940a138" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/7b/7b7f1efc19a6268f0184c1e4ebc14f0a9281d7e3fbcf788ba2c7084876b3379f.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4ee8d17-5a63-5173-8b8a-3df477a3214a" :answer/id #uuid "e4ee8d17-5a63-5173-8b8a-3df477a3214a" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/7f/7f0ad1b126502e27710bcc97a72c4eec889a74f7f6dfac6449d98710ea16e16b.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d4fc3416-aa9f-553e-b04b-84e342d586ab" :answer/id #uuid "d4fc3416-aa9f-553e-b04b-84e342d586ab" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/fa/faa4223d13523a97bd4af98d4d6014687ef3927e5c253fa8de5ca147a96f2019.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198719 :question/problem "Let $I=[0,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[0,i]\\times [0,2i].$ Which of the following represents ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the intersection of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *all* the sets:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for all}\\,\\,k\\in I}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}=[0,0.5]\\times [0,1]={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [0,0.5],b\\in [0,1]}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a rectangle whose vertices are at $(0,0),$ $(0.5,0),$ $(0.5,1),$ and $(0,1)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/5a/5a50d17270e3856778a32461449d1e1abe36376be549e460a8fcee9ef6ea194b.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[0,i]\\times [0,2i]={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [0,i],b\\in [0,2i]}\n$$\n\nis the rectangle whose vertices are at $(0,0),$ $(i,0),$ $(i,2i),$ and $(0,2i).$\n\n![](images/29/290a50d82323a459fbd0a790e28ff8889323cd5f08a0915f85b85a0aa0999490.png)\n\nThe intersection of all these rectangles is the point $(0,0):$\n\n![](images/ef/efb6d92ea0dc70fa0cbd9d82ea838b41a4eaab6ee2fc32c6fada9258a4154680.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186194940 :answer-field/correct 17592186194945 :answer-field/choices ["answer-f730d739-5d89-56ae-994d-94a686c32f0d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f730d739-5d89-56ae-994d-94a686c32f0d" :answer/id #uuid "f730d739-5d89-56ae-994d-94a686c32f0d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$∅,$ the empty set" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198532 :activity/expected-seconds 720.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
